        <mxCell id="normalization-panel" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=13;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:center&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DATABASE NORMALIZATION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;1NF — Atomic values:&lt;/b&gt; Each attribute stores a single value; no repeating groups.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;2NF — No partial dependency:&lt;/b&gt; Every non-key attribute depends on the table&#39;s primary key. The relationship data is separated into ENROLLMENTS, ATTENDANCE_RECORDS and GRADES.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;3NF — No transitive dependency:&lt;/b&gt; Non-key attributes describe their own entity and are not dependent on other non-key attributes.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;4NF — Multi-valued dependency check:&lt;/b&gt; Independent repeating academic facts are separated into ATTENDANCE_RECORDS and GRADES instead of storing multiple values in STUDENTS or COURSES.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;KEY RELATIONSHIPS / JOINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Students ↔ Enrollments ↔ Courses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Students ↔ AttendanceRecords ↔ Courses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Students ↔ Grades ↔ Courses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Example JOIN:&lt;/b&gt; Students JOIN Enrollments ON Students.StudentId = Enrollments.StudentId JOIN Courses ON Enrollments.CourseId = Courses.CourseId&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="700" x="50" y="670" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
